// The TWO gates the host opens to any guest, in its own package.
//
// Separate from `norte:plugin` for the reason in ADR 0041 decision 4: a
// package's version travels INSIDE the name of each interface
// (`norte:host/host-log@0.1.0`), so any bump of a package
// invalidates every `.wasm` artifact compiled against it — on the
// IMPORT side, empirically verified twice in `norte-plugin.wit`'s
// history. While everything lived in one package, touching `provider`
// broke the previewers.
//
// These two interfaces are the surface that moves LEAST, and every world
// imports them. Their package is versioned separately and, on purpose,
// almost never: bumping it still breaks everything, which is exactly
// what it should cost.
package norte:host@0.1.0;

/// The MINIMAL host gate (demonstrates host↔guest gating): a plugin can
/// ask the host to log a line (harmless, no capability needed) and read
/// a resource the host opened under `fs-read=scoped` (gated on the HOST).
interface host-log {
    log: func(message: string);

    /// Reads a resource the host prepared and referenced with `token`
    /// (fs-read=scoped). If the plugin did NOT declare fs-read, the host
    /// returns Err — enforcement lives in the HOST, not the guest (ADR 0022 D4).
    read-scoped: func(token: string) -> result<list<u8>, string>;
}

/// VALIDATED `[config]` settings of the plugin (P2 decision 4): the host
/// already resolved the manifest schema's defaults with `config.toml`
/// overlaid and validated (`norte-plugin-host::resolve_settings`) BEFORE
/// instantiating — the guest NEVER sees the raw `config.toml` nor decides
/// its own validity, it only reads the result. Canonical string encoding
/// (same criterion on host and guest): `bool` → `"true"`/`"false"`; `int` →
/// decimal; `string`/`enum` → the raw text.
///
/// Purely a READ over an in-memory host map: no function touches FS,
/// network or the clock (M4-P2's sandbox stays intact — this does not open a
/// new gate, it only exposes data the host had ALREADY resolved before
/// instantiating).
interface host-config {
    /// The value of `key`, or `none` if `key` is not declared in the
    /// manifest's `[config]`.
    get: func(key: string) -> option<string>;
    /// All the resolved key/value pairs (defaults + overrides).
    all: func() -> list<tuple<string, string>>;
}
